{"kfp":[{"id":"kfp","headword":"कृप्","headword_slp1":"kfp","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"1. कृ॑प् f. (only instr. कृपा॑) beautiful appearance, beauty, splendour, RV.; VS. iv, 25."}]},{"n":2,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"2. कृप् cl. 6. Ā. कृपते (impf. अकृ-पन्त; aor. 3. pl. अकृप्रन् and चकृप॑न्त, 3. sg. अक्रपिष्ट; pr. p. कृ॑पमाण),\nto mourn, long for (acc.), RV.;\nto lament, implore, RV.; AV. v, 19, 3 :\ncl. 10. P. कृपयति (impf. अकृपयत्; p. कृप॑यत् gen. sg. m. कृपयत॑स्, RV. viii, 46, 16),\nto mourn, grieve, lament (with acc.), RV.;\nto pity, BhP. viii, 7, 40;\nto be weak, Dhātup. xxxv, 17 (cf. कृपाय and √ क्रप्.)"}]}]}],"kfpaniLa":[{"id":"kfpanILa","headword":"कृपनीळ","headword_slp1":"kfpanILa","senses_r":[{"n":1,"pos":"mfn.","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"(for कृपा॑-न्˚) one whose home is splendour, dwelling in splendour (N. of Agni), RV. x, 20, 3 [‘the support of sacred rites’, Sāy.]"}]},{"n":2,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"कृप—नीळ , see s.v. 1. कृ॑प्."}]},{"n":3,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"See 1. कृ॑प्."}]}]}],"kfpanila":[{"id":"kfpAnIla","headword":"कृपानील","headword_slp1":"kfpAnIla","senses_r":[{"n":1,"pos":"m.","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"N. of a man, Saṃskārak."}]},{"n":2,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"See s.v. 1. कृ॑प्."}]},{"n":3,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"See 1. कृ॑प्."}]}]}],"kfpa":[{"id":"kfpa","headword":"कृप","headword_slp1":"kfpa","senses_r":[{"n":1,"pos":"m.","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"N. of a man (described as a friend of Indra), RV. viii, 3, 12 and 4, 2"}]},{"n":2,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"mf(ई). N. of the son and daughter of the sage Śaradvat (who performed severe penance;\nthe jealous Indra therefore sent a nymph to tempt him, but without success;\nhowever, twin sons were born to the sage in a clump of grass [शर-स्तम्बे], who were found by king Śāntanu and out of pity [कृपा] taken home and reared;\nthe daughter, Kṛpī, married Droṇa, and had by him a son called Aśvatthāman;\nthe son, Kṛpa, became one of the council at Hastināpura, and is sometimes called Gautama, sometimes Śāradvata;\naccording to Hariv. & VP., Kṛpa and Kṛpī were only distant descendants of Śaradvat;\naccording to others, Kṛpa = Vyāsa or = a son of Kṛṣṇa), MBh. &c."}]}]},{"id":"kfpA","headword":"कृपा","headword_slp1":"kfpA","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"(आ॑), f., see s.v. below."}]},{"n":2,"pos":"f. (g. भिदादि)","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"pity, tenderness, compassion (with gen. or loc.; कृपां-√ कृ, to pity [with loc.] Nal. xvii; R.), MBh. &c."}]},{"n":3,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"N. of a river (v.l. रूपा), VP."}]}]}],"kfpacarya":[{"id":"kfpAcArya","headword":"कृपाचार्य","headword_slp1":"kfpAcArya","senses_r":[{"n":1,"pos":"m.","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"N. of Gautama, Gal."}]}]}],"kfpaRa":[{"id":"kfpaRa","headword":"कृपण","headword_slp1":"kfpaRa","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"1. कृपण॑ mf(आ॑; ई, g. बह्व्-आदि)n. (gaṇas श्रेण्यादि and सुखादि, Pāṇ. viii, 2, 18; Pat.) inclined to grieve, pitiable, miserable, poor, wretched, feeble, ŚBr. xi, xiv; MBh. &c."}]},{"n":2,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"resulting from tears, AV. xi, 8, 28"}]},{"n":3,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"low, vile, W."}]},{"n":4,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"miserly, stingy, Pañcat.; Hit."}]},{"n":5,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"(अस्), m. a poor man, VarBṛS."}]},{"n":6,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"a scraper, niggard, Pañcat.; ŚārṅgP."}]},{"n":7,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"a worm, L."}]},{"n":8,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"N. of a man, VP."}]},{"n":9,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"(कृप॑णम्), n. wretchedness, misery, RV. x, 99, 9; AitBr. vii, 13; ŚāṅkhŚr.; Mn. iv, 185 &c."}]},{"n":10,"pos":"m.","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"(स-कृपणम्, ‘miserably, pitiably’), Śāntiś. (cf. कार्पण्य.)"}]},{"n":11,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"2. कृपण Nom. Ā. (3. pl. कृप॑णन्त) to long for, desire, RV. x, 74, 3."}]}]},{"id":"kfpARa","headword":"कृपाण","headword_slp1":"kfpARa","senses_r":[{"n":1,"pos":"m.","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"(Pāṇ. vii, 2, 18; Pat.) a sword, Daś.; Prab."}]},{"n":2,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"a sacrificial knife, W."}]}]}],"kfpaRa